1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,400
On television, he is the king of the dead.

2
00:00:03,930 --> 00:00:06,340
A crown of ice grows from his skull.

3
00:00:06,850 --> 00:00:09,500
He raises armies with a lift of his arms,

4
00:00:09,690 --> 00:00:14,560
and when he finally falls, every dead
thing in the world falls with him.

5
00:00:14,990 --> 00:00:16,080
But George R.

6
00:00:16,070 --> 00:00:16,220
R.

7
00:00:17,030 --> 00:00:19,620
Martin's books tell a
very different story.

8
00:00:20,630 --> 00:00:23,540
In the books, the Night's King was a man.

9
00:00:24,430 --> 00:00:28,980
A brother of the Night's Watch, who
fell in love with a woman whose skin

10
00:00:28,830 --> 00:00:33,440
was white as the moon, and whose
eyes were like blue stars.

11
00:00:35,050 --> 00:00:38,720
When it was over, his name
was erased from history.

12
00:00:39,970 --> 00:00:41,720
So who was he really?

13
00:00:47,570 --> 00:00:51,220
On the Wall stands the oldest
castle of the Night's Watch,

14
00:00:51,610 --> 00:00:52,620
and the largest.

15
00:00:53,010 --> 00:00:54,710
They call it the Nightfort.

16
00:00:55,380 --> 00:00:56,770
Its towers are broken.

17
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:00,010
Its halls are full of rats and dust.

18
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:03,620
For two hundred years, no
brother has lived there.

19
00:01:04,350 --> 00:01:07,200
When young Bran Stark shelters
inside its walls,

20
00:01:07,530 --> 00:01:11,320
he remembers the stories his old
nurse told him about this place.

21
00:01:12,050 --> 00:01:17,360
Here, the Rat Cook served a king a
pie made from the king's own son.

22
00:01:17,910 --> 00:01:22,840
Here, the seventy-nine sentinels were
sealed into the ice for deserting,

23
00:01:22,970 --> 00:01:25,940
and still stand watch, facing north.

24
00:01:26,750 --> 00:01:30,820
And here, before all of them,
Night's King had reigned,

25
00:01:30,930 --> 00:01:34,380
until his name was wiped
from the memory of man.

26
00:01:36,980 --> 00:01:39,550
The story begins at the
end of the Long Night,

27
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:41,850
a winter that lasted a generation.

28
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:47,110
When the darkness finally broke, men
raised a Wall of ice seven hundred

29
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:47,870
feet high.

30
00:01:48,580 --> 00:01:51,290
Legend says it was built
by Brandon the Builder,

31
00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:56,170
the first Stark king, with the help of
giants and the children of the forest.

32
00:01:56,570 --> 00:01:59,340
And they founded a brotherhood
to guard it.

33
00:01:59,950 --> 00:02:03,280
The Night's Watch: men who took no wives,

34
00:02:03,530 --> 00:02:06,940
held no lands, and fathered no children.

35
00:02:08,490 --> 00:02:11,860
The Night's King was the thirteenth
man to lead them.

36
00:02:12,470 --> 00:02:15,480
Old Nan said he was a warrior
who knew no fear.

37
00:02:15,950 --> 00:02:18,540
"And that was the fault
in him," she would add,

38
00:02:18,610 --> 00:02:24,920
"for all men must know fear." Fear is
what keeps a man on top of the Wall,

39
00:02:25,150 --> 00:02:26,020
watching the dark.

40
00:02:26,610 --> 00:02:31,620
A man who fears nothing might look at
the dark and want to walk into it.

41
00:02:34,210 --> 00:02:37,300
One night, from the top
of the Wall, he saw her.

42
00:02:37,570 --> 00:02:42,350
A woman with skin as white as the
moon and eyes like blue stars.

43
00:02:42,840 --> 00:02:46,170
Fearing nothing, he chased
her, and caught her,

44
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:49,490
and loved her, though her
skin was cold as ice.

45
00:02:50,180 --> 00:02:54,410
And with his love, Old Nan
said, he gave her his soul.

46
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:57,470
The books never say what she was.

47
00:02:57,920 --> 00:03:03,030
But skin like that and eyes like blue
stars are what the Others look like.

48
00:03:03,460 --> 00:03:06,510
And the tales call her the corpse queen.

49
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:10,590
He brought her back through
the Wall to the Nightfort,

50
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:14,390
and proclaimed her a queen,
and himself her king.

51
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:19,530
With strange sorceries, he bound
his sworn brothers to his will.

52
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:24,650
The men who swore to guard the realms
of men now served a king of the night.

53
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:31,440
For thirteen years, Night's King and
his corpse queen ruled the Wall.

54
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:34,990
Before we find out who brought him down,

55
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:39,530
and what they found when they did: if
you want Westeros the way Martin wrote

56
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:41,910
it, subscribe to the Mythic Archives.

57
00:03:45,110 --> 00:03:50,580
His fall took something the North had
never seen before: an alliance between

58
00:03:50,430 --> 00:03:51,120
enemies.

59
00:03:51,930 --> 00:03:55,100
The King of Winter in Winterfell,
and Joramun,

60
00:03:55,250 --> 00:03:58,000
King-beyond-the-Wall, the wildling who,

61
00:03:58,030 --> 00:04:02,800
legends say, blew the Horn of Winter
and woke giants from the earth.

62
00:04:03,330 --> 00:04:05,280
A Stark and a wildling.

63
00:04:05,910 --> 00:04:08,300
Men who had fought each
other for generations,

64
00:04:08,670 --> 00:04:11,380
now marching together against
the Watch itself.

65
00:04:12,050 --> 00:04:16,060
They broke the Night's King, and freed
his brothers from their bondage.

66
00:04:17,190 --> 00:04:20,540
Then they discovered what he had
been doing all those years.

67
00:04:21,010 --> 00:04:23,680
He had been making sacrifices
to the Others.

68
00:04:24,070 --> 00:04:26,590
So every record of him was destroyed.

69
00:04:27,260 --> 00:04:29,610
His deeds were struck from the histories.

70
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:31,810
Even his name was forbidden.

71
00:04:32,460 --> 00:04:35,070
That is why, eight thousand years later,

72
00:04:35,280 --> 00:04:37,570
nobody in Westeros knows
what he was called.

73
00:04:40,170 --> 00:04:42,000
But Old Nan had an idea.

74
00:04:42,430 --> 00:04:44,960
She always ended the story the same way.

75
00:04:45,550 --> 00:04:46,960
"Some say he was a Bolton.

76
00:04:47,370 --> 00:04:50,760
Some say a Magnar out of
Skagos, some say Umber,

77
00:04:50,990 --> 00:04:52,060
Flint, or Norrey.

78
00:04:52,490 --> 00:04:54,760
Some would have you think
he was a Woodfoot,

79
00:04:54,610 --> 00:04:59,400
from them who ruled Bear Island."
"He never was," she said.

80
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:04,750
"He was a Stark, the brother of the
man who brought him down." Then she

81
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:06,010
pinched little Bran's nose.

82
00:05:06,460 --> 00:05:09,350
"He was a Stark of Winterfell,
and who can say?

83
00:05:09,750 --> 00:05:13,700
Mayhaps his name was Brandon."
She said one more thing,

84
00:05:13,650 --> 00:05:14,940
which Bran never forgot.

85
00:05:15,350 --> 00:05:18,060
"Night's King was only
a man by light of day.

86
00:05:18,460 --> 00:05:23,230
But the night was his to rule."
It is not a strange guess.

87
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:25,770
House Stark has always loved the name.

88
00:05:26,170 --> 00:05:27,200
Brandon the Builder.

89
00:05:27,770 --> 00:05:30,740
Brandon the Shipwright, who sailed
west and never returned.

90
00:05:31,230 --> 00:05:32,910
Brandon the Burner.

91
00:05:32,760 --> 00:05:34,990
Bran's own uncle Brandon.

92
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:39,410
A Stark brother bringing
down a Stark brother.

93
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:44,340
The family whose words are "Winter is
coming" may have given the Others

94
00:05:44,190 --> 00:05:45,780
their greatest ally.

95
00:05:48,380 --> 00:05:50,690
The Nightfort still has one secret.

96
00:05:51,180 --> 00:05:55,210
In its kitchens there is an old well,
and at the bottom of the well,

97
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:56,290
there is a door.

98
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:58,990
The Watch calls it the Black Gate.

99
00:05:59,820 --> 00:06:01,370
But it isn't black at all.

100
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:05,580
It is pale white weirwood, glowing
like milk and moonlight,

101
00:06:05,710 --> 00:06:06,920
and it has a face.

102
00:06:07,690 --> 00:06:11,060
When Bran's party reaches it,
the face opens its eyes.

103
00:06:11,670 --> 00:06:13,610
"Who are you?" it asks.

104
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:19,030
A brother of the Watch, Samwell Tarly,
answers with the words of his oath.

105
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:21,370
"I am the sword in the darkness.

106
00:06:21,770 --> 00:06:23,260
I am the watcher on the walls.

107
00:06:23,660 --> 00:06:28,750
I am the shield that guards the realms
of men." "Then pass," the door says.

108
00:06:29,420 --> 00:06:32,410
Its mouth opens wide,
and they walk through,

109
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:34,310
under the Wall, into the North.

110
00:06:35,260 --> 00:06:39,590
A secret door through the Wall, in the
castle where a Lord Commander once

111
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:40,850
let the cold inside.

112
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:43,530
The books never connect the two.

113
00:06:44,180 --> 00:06:46,030
But it is hard not to wonder.

114
00:06:48,630 --> 00:06:52,420
Then, in 2014, the show gave
the name to someone new.

115
00:06:52,930 --> 00:06:57,340
In the fourth season, a White Walker rides
through the snow carrying a baby

116
00:06:57,190 --> 00:06:58,560
to an altar of ice.

117
00:06:59,070 --> 00:07:02,120
A crown of icy horns rises from his head.

118
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:05,870
He touches the child's cheek,
and its eyes turn blue.

119
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:10,370
HBO's official guide briefly
named him the Night's King,

120
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:12,470
then quietly removed the name.

121
00:07:12,870 --> 00:07:15,200
The show's version became
its great villain.

122
00:07:15,670 --> 00:07:19,680
At Hardhome, he lifts his arms
and the dead rise to join him.

123
00:07:20,150 --> 00:07:24,240
Beyond the Wall, he brings down one
of Daenerys's dragons and raises it

124
00:07:24,090 --> 00:07:24,820
as his own.

125
00:07:25,490 --> 00:07:28,040
In the sixth season, the
show reveals his origin.

126
00:07:28,770 --> 00:07:33,040
Long ago, the children of the forest bound
a man of the First Men to a weirwood

127
00:07:32,890 --> 00:07:36,220
tree and drove a blade of dragonglass
into his heart.

128
00:07:36,590 --> 00:07:38,350
He became the first White Walker.

129
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:44,190
At Winterfell, in the final season,
Arya Stark kills him with a Valyrian

130
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:47,470
steel dagger, and his entire
army falls with him.

131
00:07:47,870 --> 00:07:49,340
None of that happens in the books.

132
00:07:51,940 --> 00:07:56,050
When fans asked Martin whether the show's
Night King and the book's Night's

133
00:07:55,900 --> 00:07:59,470
King were the same person,
he gave a careful answer.

134
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:02,890
"As for the Night's King,
the form I prefer,

135
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:08,330
in the books he is a legendary figure,
akin to Lann the Clever and Brandon

136
00:08:08,180 --> 00:08:12,250
the Builder, and no more likely to have
survived to the present day than

137
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:16,590
they have." In other words, the Night's
King of the books is a legend,

138
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:20,190
like the trickster who stole Casterly
Rock and the builder of the Wall.

139
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:22,450
He may never even have existed.

140
00:08:23,020 --> 00:08:24,590
Notice the name, too.

141
00:08:25,540 --> 00:08:28,730
Martin prefers Night's King, with an S,

142
00:08:28,940 --> 00:08:29,770
like a title.

143
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:31,650
The show dropped the S.

144
00:08:31,900 --> 00:08:34,520
And the books have no Night King at all.

145
00:08:35,090 --> 00:08:38,100
No one in the novels knows
who leads the Others,

146
00:08:37,950 --> 00:08:39,760
or whether anyone does.

147
00:08:40,170 --> 00:08:42,080
No one knows where they came from.

148
00:08:42,630 --> 00:08:46,540
The children of the forest creating
them is the show's idea,

149
00:08:46,690 --> 00:08:47,700
not Martin's.

150
00:08:50,262 --> 00:08:53,632
But Martin's books are full of legends
that turn out to be real.

151
00:08:54,342 --> 00:08:58,032
In the last published novel, a strange
rider guides Bran north.

152
00:08:58,522 --> 00:09:00,532
He wears the black of the Night's Watch,

153
00:09:00,902 --> 00:09:04,052
rides a great elk, and hides
his face behind a scarf.

154
00:09:04,682 --> 00:09:07,392
His hands are black, and cold as iron.

155
00:09:07,802 --> 00:09:09,492
He cannot cross the Wall.

156
00:09:10,002 --> 00:09:12,452
"There are spells woven into it," he says,

157
00:09:12,582 --> 00:09:18,252
"old ones, and strong." The children of
the forest put it more simply: "They

158
00:09:18,102 --> 00:09:21,932
killed him long ago." Readers
call him Coldhands.

159
00:09:22,622 --> 00:09:25,392
Some believe he is a forgotten
brother of the Watch.

160
00:09:25,922 --> 00:09:28,212
A few wonder if he is something older.

161
00:09:28,782 --> 00:09:32,692
And beyond the Wall, the wildlings
have been searching for something.

162
00:09:33,222 --> 00:09:37,592
"We opened half a hundred graves,"
the wildling girl Ygritte cries,

163
00:09:37,962 --> 00:09:43,302
"and never found the Horn of Joramun."
The horn of the very king who brought

164
00:09:43,152 --> 00:09:44,462
down the Night's King.

165
00:09:45,432 --> 00:09:47,282
Martin has explained none of it.

166
00:09:47,392 --> 00:09:51,152
The Winds of Winter, the book that
should bring the Long Night,

167
00:09:51,322 --> 00:09:55,232
is still unpublished, fifteen
years after the last.

168
00:09:55,902 --> 00:10:00,132
So for now, the Night's King remains
what Old Nan made him.

169
00:10:00,422 --> 00:10:01,922
A man by day.

170
00:10:02,432 --> 00:10:03,862
A legend by night.

171
00:10:04,392 --> 00:10:08,582
And a Stark, perhaps, whose
name was Brandon.

172
00:10:09,982 --> 00:10:14,772
So, was the Night's King a traitor
who gave his soul to the enemy,

173
00:10:15,302 --> 00:10:19,032
or a man who saw the truth about
the Others before anyone else?

174
00:10:19,862 --> 00:10:21,472
Tell us what you think in the comments.

175
00:10:22,022 --> 00:10:25,392
If this story stayed with you,
give the video a like,

176
00:10:25,242 --> 00:10:27,652
and subscribe to the Mythic Archives.

177
00:10:28,052 --> 00:10:30,002
The archive is always open.
